\ examples/forth-script/parse-dump.4 - native-by-source.fth's first section, the dump read into a record,
\ in the sketch vocabulary (829): 396 characters of code where the pilot's Forth has 685 and Rill 371.
0 VALUE words  0 VALUE on  0 VALUE m
: word-line ( t --- )
  t" ^\s+(\d+)\s+(\S+)\s+(\d+) (\d+) (\d+) (\d+) (\d+) (\d+)" match TO m   m empty? IF EXIT THEN
  list[ m 1 #,  9 3 DO m I #, LOOP ]list  m 2 $@ upper  words put ;
: read-words ( --- )
  record TO words  0 TO on
  t" examples/forth-script/dump.txt" read lines texts[
    DUP t" the 3000 largest words" starts? IF DROP -1 TO on ELSE on IF word-line ELSE DROP THEN THEN
  ]texts ;
read-words words K-REC R-BOX R-JSON R-T@ TYPE CR
